Lol Nice try, but China’s poverty reduction was not a simple story of free market capitalism riding in to save the day. The state kept firm control over land ownership, banks, major industries, and the currency the whole time, and it used five year plans, state owned enterprises, and heavy government investment in infrastructure and education to drive growth. Market reforms opened space for private business, sure, but they were introduced gradually and selectively by a one party socialist government that still runs the economy today. Calling that pure capitalism is like calling a recipe “just sugar” because it has some sugar in it.

People got out of poverty because of lessened capitalism.

